    "reply": "The retrieved records cover two parts of the request: BRCA1 missense variants recorded in ClinVar and the hereditary cancer conditions linked to them. One linked condition is Hereditary breast ovarian cancer syndrome [2]. The results did not include a gene record, genetic test listings, literature, or the clinical significance of these variants.\n\n## Associated conditions\n\nHereditary breast ovarian cancer syndrome is one linked condition [2]. Hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome is another [4]. Familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1 is also represented [12].\n\n## ClinVar missense variants\n\nAll the variants are annotated on the NM_007294.4 transcript, and they span the coding sequence from the N-terminal region to the C-terminal region. Near the N-terminus, ClinVar:1001081 is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.353T>C (p.Leu118Pro) [5]. Another N-terminal variant, ClinVar:1009204, is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.500C>T (p.Thr167Ile) [24]. In the central region, ClinVar:1000551 is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.3664G>A (p.Glu1222Lys) [3]. Toward the C-terminus, ClinVar:1000183 is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.4709T>C (p.Leu1570Pro) [1]. Another C-terminal variant, ClinVar:1005528, is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.4685C>G (p.Pro1562Arg) [15].\n\n## Proline and cysteine changes\n\nSeveral substitutions introduce or remove proline or cysteine residues. ClinVar:1003072 is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.3017A>C (p.His1006Pro) [8]. ClinVar:1005082 is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.1930T>G (p.Cys644Gly) [14]. ClinVar:1009310 is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.3673T>A (p.Cys1225Ser) [26].",
